<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin confident amid possible U.S. hike.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin confident amid possible U.S. hike.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Friday that with the exception of youth unemployment, he was confident the Canadian economy could withstand a possible hike in U.S. interest rates next week.</p>
<p>&quot;The Canadian economy is right now certainly running on all cylinders,&quot; Martin told reporters. &quot;But as we have said, there is one indicator that is missing and that is youth unemployment and that's what we have to got to focus on,&quot; Martin said outside the House of Commons.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
